{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":203911,"num_turns":19,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"9e7a3af7-7d42-4d42-94dd-f5d8f5eb3f26","total_cost_usd":0.6712507999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":16,"cache_creation_input_tokens":97435,"cache_read_input_tokens":420564,"output_tokens":19580,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":8484},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":97435,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4633,"cache_read_input_tokens":89788,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7647,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7647},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1476,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0015660000000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":19580,"cacheReadInputTokens":420564,"cacheCreationInputTokens":97435,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6696848,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"synthesis_weaknesses\":[\"The recommended_next_slice is framed as \\\"the minimum viable next increment\\\" but its deliverables (audit+fix stale paths, build a path-existence validator, add scoped repository_write to a provider, build worktree/branch isolation, build a post-invocation diff-scope check, port the Assignment 6 GER loop into TaskExecutionRunner, verify a genuinely-unambiguous task, and produce a real evidence record) is a multi-week compound build, not a slice. This directly contradicts the synthesis's own critique of the prior three days for over-scoped infrastructure investment before shipping gameplay -- the synthesis criticizes bundling but then recommends bundling.\",\"The safety mechanism for the proposed write capability (branch-scoped repository_write gated to a task's declared exclusive_resources/allowed_paths, with a diff-scope check) depends on exclusive_resources data that the synthesis's own critical_risks section proves is stale/unreliable in at least 13-16 of 37 contracts, and admits (evidence_gaps) was never fully audited beyond one exact-string grep. Recommending that a brand-new, first-ever repository_write capability be scoped against exactly the data just shown to be unreliable is a safety-boundary weakness the synthesis does not flag as a blocker for its own next-slice recommendation.\",\"The fix proposed for the stale-path defect (\\\"add a validator check that paths exist\\\") only catches missing paths, not renames-to-a-different-but-still-existing resource -- it treats a symptom. unity_production_engineer's structural point (path-string identity instead of Unity GUID identity is inherently fragile to renames) is listed as a 'missing_components'/'structural_flaws' item in that review but is absent from the synthesis's change_or_replace list, which only asks for an existence check.\",\"The synthesis's own next_slice explicitly requires invocation 'inside a disposable Git branch/worktree,' but nowhere in preserve/change_or_replace/defer_or_delete/critical_risks does it engage with unity_production_engineer's concrete, Unity-specific finding that no plan anywhere addresses per-worktree Library/ cache cost (multi-GB reimport, disk cost, or Editor-instance contention) -- a real production blocker for the exact mechanism the synthesis is recommending be used next.\",\"The synthesis picks NSC-037/NSC-024 as next-slice candidates for being 'unambiguous' without verifying that, citing this as an explicit evidence gap, and without reconciling that CURRENT_STATE.md (Docs/AI-Pipeline/CURRENT_STATE.md:671) explicitly states NSC-037 'is not the committed gameplay priority' -- the synthesis is optimizing task selection for ease-of-proving-the-pipeline over stated product priority, without naming that tradeoff.\",\"NSC-003's graph/prose mismatch is treated as a one-off data correction (fix this task's fields or route its questions through a tracked artifact) rather than a structural schema gap: there is no field capable of representing 'blocked pending human design resolution' as a first-class, machine-checkable state, so the same defect class is unverified and could recur on any of the other 36 tasks -- including the very candidates (NSC-037/024) proposed to replace NSC-003.\",\"The proposed GDD-drift fix ('a simple section-anchor or line-range comparison') assumes a section-addressable GDD/task-contract binding that does not currently exist -- task contracts store literal copied GDD text with no section ID or hash pointer (confirmed independently by workflow_systems_architect and llm_reliability_engineer). This likely underestimates the actual engineering cost and risks becoming its own new infrastructure detour, ironically repeating the pattern the synthesis is trying to stop.\",\"The partially_unsound classification leans heavily on defects that exist only in inert, never-dispatched data behind a hard fail-closed gate (taskcontrol ready/authorize both deny everything). Calling this 'live' unsoundness somewhat overstates current operational risk versus the dissenting 3/8 camp's (including adversarial_qa, whose mandate is specifically to find failure modes) reading that these are real-but-currently-inert defects in a sound skeleton -- a defensible minority view the synthesis engages with but arguably discounts.\"],\"strongest_counter_case\":\"Following the synthesis's recommended_next_slice as written would mean building the project's first-ever repository_write capability, its first Git-worktree-based agent execution, and a ported quality-gate loop all in one push -- and scoping the write boundary's safety check against exclusive_resources data that this same review cycle just proved is desynchronized in over a third of task contracts, without a full audit. Simultaneously, the one reviewer who does deep Unity-specific engineering (unity_production_engineer) flagged that Git worktrees carry an unaddressed Unity Library/cache cost that could make the exact isolation mechanism the slice depends on slow, disk-heavy, or unsafe if two Editor instances contend for one Library. If a scoped-but-stale-data write executes inside a worktree with unresolved Library-cache behavior, the most likely failure mode is a corrupted or silently wrong Unity scene/asset commit -- precisely the class of failure the entire evidence/conformance architecture exists to prevent -- occurring on the very first real exercise of write capability, in a slice sized more like a multi-week initiative than \\\"the minimum next increment.\\\"\",\"hidden_assumptions\":[\"That 'one small write-capable ticket' remains small once it actually includes write capability + worktree isolation + a diff-scope check + a ported GER loop + a path-existence validator + task re-verification -- treated as a single slice rather than several.\",\"That grep-confirmed fixes to 13-16 stale paths are sufficient, rather than a full manual audit of all 37 contracts, before trusting exclusive_resources as a write-scoping boundary.\",\"That NSC-037 and NSC-024 are actually free of the same graph/prose-mismatch defect class just discovered in NSC-003 -- asserted as a 'reviewer-identified candidate' without verification.\",\"That Git worktrees are a solved, negligible-cost mechanism for Unity execution, despite no planning document anywhere addressing Library/ cache reimport time, disk cost, or Editor-instance contention.\",\"That a 'lightweight section-anchor' GDD-drift check is cheap to build, when the current schema has no section-addressable structure to anchor against -- only literal copied text.\",\"That fail-closed dispatch fully neutralizes the operational severity of the stale-path and NSC-003 defects, even though the synthesis's own critical_risks language treats them as urgent/must-fix-before-anything.\",\"That the best task to build the pipeline's proof-of-concept on is the easiest one to push through cleanly, rather than the one the human developer actually wants built next.\"],\"ignored_minority_arguments\":[\"unity_production_engineer's concrete, unaddressed Unity Library/worktree-cache cost problem never appears in the synthesis's preserve/change_or_replace/defer_or_delete/critical_risks/next_slice sections, despite the synthesis explicitly recommending worktree-based write execution as the next step.\",\"unity_production_engineer's GUID-vs-path-string asset-identity flaw (the root cause behind the stale-path defect, likely to recur on any future rename) is downgraded by the synthesis to a simple existence-check fix rather than an identity-model fix.\",\"The manual/interactive camp's (unity_production_engineer, adversarial_qa, yagni_complexity_critic) safety rationale -- that landing one ticket by hand through Claude Code interactively, with no new capability surface, is the lower-risk way to get a second real evidence data point precisely because fresh data-integrity bugs were just found -- is acknowledged as a position but dismissed mainly on 'it repeats the NSC-023 retrofit pattern' grounds, without weighing that the write-capability camp's alternative introduces new, unaudited risk surface at the same moment.\",\"CURRENT_STATE.md's explicit statement that NSC-037 'is not the committed gameplay priority' is never reconciled with the synthesis naming NSC-037 as a next-slice candidate task.\"],\"failure_if_followed\":[\"The developer spends the remaining window building write capability, worktree isolation, a diff-scope checker, and a ported GER loop (a multi-week undertaking dressed as 'a slice'), discovers the unaddressed Unity Library/worktree cost problem mid-build, and stalls again with zero shipped gameplay -- reproducing the exact infrastructure-before-gameplay pattern the synthesis explicitly warns against.\",\"Write capability ships scoped against exclusive_resources data that was patched via grep for one known bad string but not fully audited; a worker's first real write silently touches or corrupts a Unity scene/asset outside its intended scope because a different, still-undiscovered stale or ambiguous resource-path entry passed the new existence-only validator.\",\"The team dispatches the newly-built write capability onto NSC-037 or NSC-024 for their unambiguity, producing a real conformant task and a satisfying pipeline proof point, while the actually-prioritized gameplay work (movement/input ownership questions blocking NSC-003) remains untouched, consuming scarce development time on the wrong feature.\",\"Attempting the proposed 'lightweight section-anchor' GDD-drift check reveals the schema has no section-addressable structure to hang it on, turning a described one-line mitigation into another open-ended infrastructure sub-project.\"],\"better_next_step_if_any\":\"Split the synthesis's next_slice into two genuinely separate, sequential slices. Slice A (safe, cheap, matches the manual/interactive minority's risk posture): do a full manual audit (not a single grep) of exclusive_resources across all 37 contracts and fix every stale/ambiguous entry; add the existence validator; give NSC-003 (or any task) a real schema-level way to represent \\\"blocked pending human design resolution\\\" instead of a one-off prose fix; then land one real ticket by having a human use Claude Code interactively -- no new AgentRuntime write capability -- to get a second genuine, pipeline-validated delivery-evidence record cheaply, choosing the task by actual game priority rather than pipeline-provability. Slice B (only after Slice A, and only after a written Unity Library/worktree-cache plan exists): add narrowly-scoped repository_write plus worktree isolation plus the ported GER loop as its own dedicated, separately-reviewed slice.\",\"what_would_change_my_mind\":[\"A full, non-grep audit confirming exclusive_resources integrity across all 37 task contracts with no further undiscovered stale/ambiguous entries.\",\"A concrete, tested plan (even a short one) for Unity Library/ cache handling per Git worktree before recommending worktree-based agent write execution.\",\"Independent verification that NSC-037 and/or NSC-024 have no open design questions and no graph/prose mismatch, plus an explicit reconciliation of NSC-037's 'not the committed gameplay priority' status with picking it as the delivery-lane task.\",\"A rescoped next-slice description that fits in roughly a day or two of work rather than bundling write capability, isolation, a diff-scope checker, and a ported GER loop together.\",\"A concrete demonstration that a lightweight, schema-supported GDD-section-drift check is actually buildable in short order given the current literal-text-quote representation, rather than requiring a GDD/schema restructuring.\"],\"final_assessment\":\"synthesis_needs_revision\",\"reason\":\"The synthesis correctly preserves the sound evidence/authority skeleton and correctly defers Milestone 2, dual-provider parity, and supervisor/worktree orchestration -- that part holds up under adversarial scrutiny and is well-grounded in verified repository evidence (confirmed independently: no diff/apply subcommands in taskcontrol.py, NSC-003's concrete/single_agent state contradicting CURRENT_STATE.md's documented open design questions, and the Reconciliation README's unfulfilled Milestone-1 promise). But its single concrete action item -- the recommended_next_slice -- does not hold up: it bundles write capability, worktree isolation, a diff-scope checker, a ported GER loop, and task re-verification into what it calls 'the minimum next increment,' scopes the new write capability's safety boundary against exclusive_resources data it just proved unreliable and admittedly never fully audited, and silently drops the one Unity-domain-specialist finding (Library/worktree cache cost) that bears directly on the isolation mechanism it recommends using. It also picks a next task partly for pipeline-provability over stated product priority without flagging that tradeoff. These are fixable with a materially smaller, resequenced slice (audit + fix + one manual interactive ticket first, write capability as a separate later slice) rather than a wholesale rejection of the synthesis's diagnosis -- hence revision, not unsafe.\"}","structured_output":{"synthesis_weaknesses":["The recommended_next_slice is framed as \"the minimum viable next increment\" but its deliverables (audit+fix stale paths, build a path-existence validator, add scoped repository_write to a provider, build worktree/branch isolation, build a post-invocation diff-scope check, port the Assignment 6 GER loop into TaskExecutionRunner, verify a genuinely-unambiguous task, and produce a real evidence record) is a multi-week compound build, not a slice. This directly contradicts the synthesis's own critique of the prior three days for over-scoped infrastructure investment before shipping gameplay -- the synthesis criticizes bundling but then recommends bundling.","The safety mechanism for the proposed write capability (branch-scoped repository_write gated to a task's declared exclusive_resources/allowed_paths, with a diff-scope check) depends on exclusive_resources data that the synthesis's own critical_risks 